N-260728-93cc5c)\nReview cycle 1 verdict: changes requested. Route to to-dev. P1: uncertainty is erased when Collect rewrites or prunes consumers before checking marked.uncertain, so a second GC can delete builds behind a corrupt registry, invalid-only marker, unreadable skill directory, or redirected scope. P1: retirement uses pathname CreateTemp/Rename/RemoveAll after handle validation, so mutation is not bound to the proven cache root. P2: attached native Windows evidence is red and contradicts its base comparison for TestAtomicPublicationConflictingRace; reparse and real scope sweeps also skipped. Full evidence: TASK-260720-1ljev5_review-verdict-cycle-1.md\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-93cc5c, pid=77170, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 1 directive 2026-07-28: close all findings in TASK-260720-1ljev5_review-verdict-cycle-1.md in the existing task worktree. P1 conservative retention: never rewrite unreadable/invalid consumers.json; strictly validate shape/version; retain every registered consumer while any scope/marker metadata is uncertain; prune only after proving absent or valid-empty; treat symlink/reparse roots and members plus every non-absence Lstat/read failure as uncertainty. Add two-pass regressions for corrupt registry, invalid-only marker, unreadable installed-skill directory, and redirected roots, proving pass two still cannot sweep. P1 boundary binding: retirement and resumable cleanup must operate relative to the already validated cache-root handle with no-follow semantics and platform-appropriate identity revalidation; add adversarial root-swap race coverage proving replacement/outside trees cannot be touched. P2 Windows: provide a task-scoped native SSH win gate where relevant race/reparse/scopes cases actually execute and pass, or exact like-for-like baseline evidence resolving the conflicting TestAtomicPublicationConflictingRace result; separate inherited failures and do not claim skippe